Chapter: CtorNarrowWarn

 Regression guard for FabledTreasureMap entry 11, suppression side:
 an explicit __narrow at a bounded ctor payload takes responsibility
 for the range with a runtime trap, so the construction compiles
 clean. The rejected unnarrowed twin lives in errors/
 narrowing-unproven, since CDX2051 became an error. The expected
 sidecar pins the in-range runtime behavior.

Section: Definitions

  Byteish =
   | MkByte (Integer between 0 and 255)

  use-byte : Byteish -> Integer
  use-byte (b) = when b
   is MkByte (v) -> v

  make-byte-narrowed : Integer -> Byteish
  make-byte-narrowed (n) = MkByte (__narrow n)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (use-byte (make-byte-narrowed 42)))
  end
